questions.answer:
S25 is the old comparison-distribution idea from 2026-06-11: a bare value after a comparator reused that comparator. The owner has now clarified and ratified the cleanup: boolean `||`/`&&` do NOT distribute comparisons. Comparator alternatives use single `|`.

Retired old spelling:

    status == 400 || 404

Canonical arm-head spelling:

    if status == {
        400 | 404 -> handle_client_error()
        500 | 503 -> handle_server_error()
        else -> handle_other()
    }

Explicit comparator arm-head spelling:

    if status {
        status == 400 | 404 -> handle_client_error()
        else -> handle_other()
    }

So `|` separates value/pattern alternatives against the comparator. `||`, `&&`, `==`, and `!=` remain boolean arm condition/guard syntax.
